WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.352
Hey, Dreamer here.

4
00:00:09.352 --> 00:00:16.099
The AI tab, part two: the jobs that make up characters, run their chats, and decide what they do.

5
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.453
Open the AI tab, then New NPC.

6
00:00:19.453 --> 00:00:25.312
This one makes up the characters the story needs on the fly, and it only has a custom box.

7
00:00:25.312 --> 00:00:27.852
Ours lists what every new person needs,

8
00:00:27.852 --> 00:00:32.930
how names sound depending on where they're from, and how tough they should be.

9
00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:40.132
NPC Chat Replies is how a character answers when a player chats with them directly.

10
00:00:40.132 --> 00:00:46.489
The default treats it like a text chat: a sentence or two, unless the player asks for more.

11
00:00:46.933 --> 00:00:52.436
Our custom is how show folk and townsfolk talk, and the one thing nobody talks about.

12
00:00:53.833 --> 00:00:59.383
When a chat ends, NPC Chat Summary writes a few sentences about it back into the story.

13
00:00:59.833 --> 00:01:04.826
Ours makes sure promises, money and rumours always get carried forward.

14
00:01:06.233 --> 00:01:12.338
NPC Details fills in the characters the AI makes up: their public description,

15
00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:16.252
hidden info, personality and more, a section each.

16
00:01:16.252 --> 00:01:18.052
This one's hidden info.

17
00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:22.067
Our custom: everyone in town has an opinion of the show,

18
00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:28.183
and in towns the Gilt Circus has worked, their hidden info says whether Gilt money reached them.

19
00:01:29.567 --> 00:01:33.174
NPC Intents decides what characters try to do in a fight.

20
00:01:33.174 --> 00:01:39.249
Out of the box it only works in combat, and outside a fight it leaves the scene to the narrator.

21
00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:45.185
Ours says townsfolk run before they fight, bandits run once two of them drop,

22
00:01:45.185 --> 00:01:48.605
and Bramble only ever swats, and only over food.

23
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:55.471
NPC Updates runs after each turn and moves relationship scores.

24
00:01:55.471 --> 00:02:00.855
By default a score only shifts for real, face-to-face moments.

25
00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:07.209
Ours sets what joining the party means in our world: leaving the show to go with the player.

26
00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:13.381
Worth knowing: New NPC and NPC Details work on the characters the AI makes up.

27
00:02:13.381 --> 00:02:18.898
Chats, fight intents and relationship updates apply to everyone, your own people included.

28
00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:21.917
That's the people side.

29
00:02:21.917 --> 00:02:25.221
Our instructions are linked in the description.

30
00:02:25.221 --> 00:02:30.494
Next time, the world side: items, learned abilities, encounters and places.

31
00:02:30.933 --> 00:02:34.881
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

